# Names a public page cites although tracked code does not spell them. One per line; the reason goes above each group.

# Positional arguments of `poot-serve`, placeholders in the configuration table.
MODEL
ADDR
# Settings the batching and tensor-parallel pages say the server does not read yet.
POOT_MAX_BATCHED_TOKENS
POOT_TP_GPUS
# A commit of an earlier benchmark snapshot.
a39b146b
# Other projects' and papers' names (models, libraries, venues, APIs, tools, ELF constants).
NumPy
OpenXLA
NeurIPS
RoFormer
SmolVLM
GeLU
SiLU
PagedAttention
BlinkMacSystemFont
donate_argnums
cuStreamBeginCapture
amdclang
__ocml_exp_f32
PT_AMDGPU_HSA_LOAD_GLOBAL_DATA
PT_AMDGPU_HSA_LOAD_KERNEL_ARGUMENT
# SPIR-V memory-semantics name the Vulkan post-process rewrites barriers to; the code spells it only in comments.
AcquireRelease
# A file the `pootc` build writes, not a tracked one.
poot_cache.rs
# Names of wgpu's and LLVM's own API and memory-ordering terms, cited when the pages describe the backend path.
ComputePipeline
SeqCst
# The vendor's family name in prose; the code spells the family `minimax_m2` and `MiniMaxM2`.
MiniMax
# A ggml tensor type poot deliberately has no format for; the pages name it as an example of a refused type.
Q8_K
# Theme CSS custom properties (--poot-*) and the monospace font name in website/src/css and the homepage CSS (upstream PR #1); not crates or code identifiers.
poot-accent
poot-coral
poot-ink
poot-line
poot-surface
JetBrains
